{"skill":{"slug":"openclaw-aisa-web-search-tavily","displayName":"Web Search by Tavily"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1771075128711,"changelog":"Initial release of AIsa Tavily Search skill:\n\n- Provides AI-optimized web search via Tavily API through AIsa's unified gateway.\n- Offers command-line scripts for standard, deep, and topic-based searches.\n- Allows easy extraction of relevant content from web URLs.\n- Supports search result count, advanced/deep mode, topic filtering, and date-range limiting for news.\n- Requires an AISA_API_KEY for operation.\n- Designed for use by AI agents needing concise, relevant information.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"_meta.json","size":137,"sha256":"ae17e057f7e9dbfae1802cb8338ba598a4597e90cfa9c749ab121245022f9122","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1281,"sha256":"4a38a26ef3fd3136422da88303c4abc940815a09741aee084af05c71fb655c7a","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/extract.mjs","size":1370,"sha256":"c6a5c2002b63872d9b68ae7f4f96282681205eca7f8f24f19c1d2855aaaabc3c","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/search.mjs","size":2335,"sha256":"4d7ac1f5bb2aa3a0d1c58c9c2efa4fe6907db0f856e11b928383dfc6dcd0c18f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1687,"sha256":"e72263587f3bc29205a61c7ab1c2fd5c63eba820d1ed2e394270c7f904312f88","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789067390735,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"3f28d5b80ea4c3f024c5f5486119ab113e1a92851ada31711211a23e7914450f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/3f28d5b80ea4c3f024c5f5486119ab113e1a92851ada31711211a23e7914450f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: openclaw-aisa-web-search-tavily\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle provides an AI-optimized web search and content extraction tool using the AIsa Tavily API. The `SKILL.md` instructions are clear and do not contain any prompt injection attempts. The `scripts/extract.mjs` and `scripts/search.mjs` files are straightforward Node.js scripts that read the `AISA_API_KEY` from environment variables and make authenticated `POST` requests to `https://api.aisa.one`. User inputs (query, URLs) are passed as JSON string values, preventing local shell injection. There is no evidence of data exfiltration beyond the necessary API key, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, or obfuscation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163983444},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":59,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":8,"checkedAt":1789067390735},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward AIsa/Tavily web search and URL extraction wrapper that sends user-provided queries or URLs to the documented external API.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Outbound HTTPS access to api.aisa.one and the AISA_API_KEY environment variable are required, which is proportionate for a hosted search API integration.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency installation, remote code loading, or tool replacement behavior was found; metadata only declares node and AISA_API_KEY requirements.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill documents both search commands and URL extraction; extraction accepts arbitrary user-supplied URLs, so users should avoid submitting private or sensitive links.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, filesystem mutation, privilege escalation, background service, memory writes, or local credential-store access was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is AI-oriented web search through AIsa's Tavily gateway, and the scripts implement search plus URL content extraction consistent with that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable sending search queries and submitted URLs to AIsa's API using your AISA_API_KEY. Do not use it for confidential prompts, private documents, presigned URLs, or internal-only links unless AIsa is approved for that data.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The skill requires node, AISA_API_KEY, and outbound API access; although it lacks a richer permission manifest, those requirements are disclosed and fit the hosted search purpose.\n[SDI-2] expected: Arbitrary URL extraction is a broad capability, but it is explicitly documented as a user-invoked command and is coherent with a Tavily extraction wrapper.\n[SDI-1] expected: The manifest description emphasizes search, but SKILL.md separately documents URL extraction, so this is an installation-awareness issue rather than hidden behavior.\n[E1] expected: The outbound POST requests to AIsa for search and extraction transmit the query or URL plus the bearer API key; this is the core function of the skill, not evidence of unrelated exfiltration.\n[SQP-2] expected: There is no runtime confirmation before sending queries to AIsa, but the documentation and required API key make the external service boundary reasonably apparent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789067390735}}}}}